<xml>
  <block type="ll_i2c_device" x="25" y="25">
    <mutation uid="raw_sensor" />
    <field name="NAME">sensor</field>
    <field name="ADDR">0x68</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Purpose: Read an I2C register using a named device address.
Hardware: use Connections to check pin ownership for your selected board. Open the comment bubbles on the main steps for explanations.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="25" y="100">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="controls_if">
        <value name="IF0">
          <block type="ll_i2c_config">
            <value name="HZ">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">100000</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="TIMEOUT">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">25000</field>
              </block>
            </value>
          </block>
        </value>
        <statement name="DO0">
          <block type="serial_print">
            <value name="CONTENT">
              <block type="text">
                <field name="TEXT">I2C ready: WHO_AM_I register read</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
          </block>
        </statement>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Runs once after power-on or reset. Initialise the program here; repeating measurements and animation belong in loop.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="600" y="25">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="ll_i2c_start">
        <field name="DEVICE">raw_sensor</field>
        <next>
          <block type="ll_i2c_write">
            <field name="DEVICE">raw_sensor</field>
            <value name="VALUE">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">117</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
                <field name="TYPE">uint8_t</field>
                <field name="VAR">status</field>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="ll_i2c_end">
                    <field name="DEVICE">raw_sensor</field>
                    <value name="STOP">
                      <block type="logic_boolean">
                        <field name="BOOL">FALSE</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="controls_if">
                    <value name="IF0">
                      <block type="logic_compare">
                        <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                        <value name="A">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">status</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="B">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">0</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <statement name="DO0">
                      <block type="arduino_typed_variable">
                        <field name="TYPE">uint8_t</field>
                        <field name="VAR">received</field>
                        <value name="VALUE">
                          <block type="ll_i2c_request">
                            <field name="DEVICE">raw_sensor</field>
                            <value name="COUNT">
                              <block type="math_number">
                                <field name="NUM">1</field>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                            <value name="STOP">
                              <block type="logic_boolean">
                                <field name="BOOL">TRUE</field>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <next>
                          <block type="controls_if">
                            <value name="IF0">
                              <block type="logic_compare">
                                <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                                <value name="A">
                                  <block type="variables_get">
                                    <field name="VAR">received</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                                <value name="B">
                                  <block type="math_number">
                                    <field name="NUM">1</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                            <statement name="DO0">
                              <block type="ll_serial_number">
                                <field name="BASE">HEX</field>
                                <field name="END">println</field>
                                <value name="VALUE">
                                  <block type="ll_i2c_read">
                                    <field name="DEVICE">raw_sensor</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                              </block>
                            </statement>
                            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
                          </block>
                        </next>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create received as uint8_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </statement>
                    <next>
                      <block type="serial_print">
                        <value name="CONTENT">
                          <block type="text">
                            <field name="TEXT">I2C status (0=OK):</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <next>
                          <block type="ll_serial_number">
                            <field name="BASE">DEC</field>
                            <field name="END">println</field>
                            <value name="VALUE">
                              <block type="variables_get">
                                <field name="VAR">status</field>
                              </block>
                            </value>
                            <next>
                              <block type="base_delay">
                                <value name="DELAY_TIME">
                                  <block type="math_number">
                                    <field name="NUM">1000</field>
                                  </block>
                                </value>
                                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Wait for the given number of milliseconds (1000 ms = 1 second). This pauses the main program; avoid long waits when loop must service motors, music files or serial input.</comment>
                              </block>
                            </next>
                          </block>
                        </next>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </next>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
                  </block>
                </next>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create status as uint8_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeats until power is removed. Each block runs in order, then execution returns to the top. Keep this loop responsive when servicing motors, music or serial input.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
